    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's a debate, but it feels like people on both sides just use different stats to prove themselves right. if you look at the actual history, doesn't the risk of capital flight usually end up being the deciding factor? like, if the money isn't there to invest, does it even matter if inequality goes down a bit?",
